LabCairn — third-party notices
===============================================================================

Applies to: the `labcairn` 0.1.0 source distribution and wheel.

Measured: 2026-10-25, by building the artefacts (`uv build`), reading their
member lists and their bytes, and reading the licence of every installed
dependency out of its own installed distribution metadata. The dependency
figures below come from the `uv.lock` at commit dd08573.

Every number in this file was measured rather than remembered. §5 gives the
commands that reproduce them.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0.  This file is a notice, not a licence
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

It records the third-party material that travels with a LabCairn distribution
and the terms each item travels under.

It grants no rights, and it asserts no licence for LabCairn itself.
LICENSE.PENDING.md says in its own first line: "This file is not a license.
It is a notice that no license has been granted." Nothing here changes that.
The copyright in LabCairn is unresolved, so no statement in this file may be
read as a claim that LabCairn is open source. The root licence that a future
release would carry is the copyright owner's to grant, and this file is not
where that grant is made.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.  What a LabCairn distribution contains
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Measured from the built artefacts:

  source distribution (labcairn-0.1.0.tar.gz)
      the repository's committed file list, plus the one file the build
      backend adds, PKG-INFO
  wheel (labcairn-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl)
      the 147 files under src/labcairn, plus six .dist-info metadata members
      (METADATA, RECORD, WHEEL, entry_points.txt, licenses/LICENSE.PENDING.md
      and this NOTICE)

The exact member counts for the release as built are in
docs/acceptance/LC-P1-14-release-contents.md. The release workflow re-measures
both lists on every run and fails if either artefact carries a member the
committed tree does not, or is missing one the tree has.

Two things follow, and both are checked by the release workflow rather than
asserted here:

  * No third-party source code is vendored into either artefact. Every member
    is a file of this repository.

  * The runtime dependencies are NOT redistributed in either artefact. The
    wheel's metadata names them (Requires-Dist) and the installer fetches
    each one as its own distribution, under its own licence and carrying its
    own notices. Section 2 is about what arrives that way.

The only third-party files the distribution carries as files are the three
papers in §4.


