-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.  What LabCairn's own reports carry, and how to reproduce this file
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5.1  The reports carry no font
-------------------------------

LabCairn's own artefacts carry no font file: the wheel's 153 members include
none whose name is a font file, and the source distribution's only members
holding font binaries are the three papers of §4.

The report forms carry none either. The PDF exporter references the Type 1
core faces and embeds nothing — /FontFile, /FontFile2 and /FontFile3 are
absent and /FontDescriptor appears zero times; the DOCX exporter names fonts
in word/fontTable.xml and ships no part under word/fonts/; the figure is a
raster, so its text is pixels. Both properties are watched by tests, not only
asserted here: tests/test_analysis_report_render.py::test_the_pdf_embeds_no_font
and ::test_the_docx_embeds_no_font.

5.2  Reproducing the numbers
------------------------------

  uv build
    # then list the two member lists, and diff the sdist's against the tree:
    tar -tzf dist/labcairn-0.1.0.tar.gz | grep -v '/$' | sed 's|^labcairn-0.1.0/||' | LC_ALL=C sort
    git ls-tree -r --name-only HEAD | LC_ALL=C sort
    python -c "import zipfile;print('\n'.join(sorted(zipfile.ZipFile('dist/labcairn-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl').namelist())))"

  # the dependency closure and its licences:
  uv export --frozen --no-dev --no-hashes --no-emit-project --format requirements.txt
  uv venv --python 3.12 .release-audit
  uv pip install --python .release-audit -r <that export>
  .release-audit/bin/python -c "..."   # read each distribution's own metadata

The release workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml) runs the same audit on
every run, and fails if a dependency's licence is not one the NOTICE records,
if the closure resolves to a different set than the lockfile names, or if
either artefact stops carrying this file.
